<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Lovrijenac</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fort St Lawrence</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Lovrijenac (St Lawrence) is a fortress standing on a sea cliff 37 metres high just outside the western walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubrovnik">Dubrovnik</a>. Built in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and strengthened in the fifteenth and sixteenth centuries, it guarded the city's western approaches by land and sea against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. Its gate bears the inscription Non bene pro toto libertas venditur auro, meaning that freedom is not to be sold for all the gold in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-lovrijenac.jpg" alt="Fort Lovrijenac" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raki_Man · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:City_Walls_-_panoramio_-_Raki_Man.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
